|-
!<center>[[Image:icon-ana.png|80px|link=Ana]]<br />[[Ana]]</center>
|'''<nowiki>HIGH PRIORITY  |  EXTREMELY HIGH RISK</nowiki>'''


Ana is extremely painful to play against. With her Biotic Grenade and Sleep Dart, you will be unable to receive the healing outcome from Cardiac Overdrive and make you become a easy prey for enemy team. Not to mention, Poke is one of Mauga's greatest weakness and she will be bound to slowly chip down Mauga's health. Without these tools, though, she is an extremely vulnerable target and easy to takedown. If possible, look to use Overrun and slam on top of her, and use Chainguns to finish her off before she can get back up.


Their Perks - Groggy is VERY annoying, and very theatening for Mauga as one of his primary weaknesses is being slowed. Headhunter can also cause a lot of pre-fight damage to Mauga. Biotic Bounce can reapply anti-heal and deal extra damage.


Your Perks - Pyromaniac is a must here. You need as much sustain as possible. Firewalker can also help finish a kill on an Ana if you slam her with Overrun. Combat Fuel can be used to minimize Anti-heal effects a ''little,'' but it's not great against her.

|'''GOOD SYNERGY'''
Ana's Biotic Grenade enables Mauga to have some insane healing number while using Cardiac Overdrive, and Sleep Dart allows an easy Overrun stomp. Nano-boost, is well, nano-boost. It makes Mauga's damage output insane. If she has Speed Serum as a perk, it makes Mauga's Overrun INSANELY fast, allowing him to basically teleport into the enemy team's backline if he wants.

|-
!<center>[[Image:icon-baptiste.png|80px|link=Baptiste]]<br />[[Baptiste]]</center>
|'''<nowiki>EXTREMELY HIGH PRIORITY  |  MEDIUM RISK</nowiki>'''


While Baptiste has good long range damage, he does not have any form of CC or status effects to apply. The only thing he has against Mauga is his Exo-Boots, enabling him to escape to high ground. If there is no high ground available, he becomes a very easy target to run down and shred. Be careful of his Immortality field, especially when it's used on his teammates.


Their Perks - None of Baptiste's perks have an major effect on Mauga, besides his Rocket Boots, allowing him some horizontal mobility to escape Mauga.


Your Perks - Pyromaniac is good against Baptiste, due to his lack of protection and relatively large hitbox for a support. Firewalker is very good against Baptiste, as the status effect can be applied to Immortality Field and help destroy it quicker, and most comps with a Baptiste will play fairly stacked.

|'''EXCEPTIONAL SYNERGY'''

''"You and me Baptiste, You and Me."'' 

These two are like bread and butter. Baptiste has insanely high sustain to keep a Mauga alive in a teamfight, and with Immortality Field, allow Mauga to survive things he normally couldn't, such as high burst damage or status effects. Cage Fight and Amplification Matrix can be used in tandem to create an area of death for the enemy team, trapping them into a zone while being pelted on with massive damage from the Matrix. 

|-
!<center>[[Image:icon-brigitte.png|80px|link=Brigitte]]<br />[[Brigitte]]</center>
|'''<nowiki>EXTREMELY HIGH PRIORITY  |  LOW RISK</nowiki>'''
Brigitte is an exceptionally easy target to eliminate as Mauga. While she can block your damage using her barrier, it is very low HP and reduces her move speed, allowing for an easy slam with Overrun. The only way a Brigitte can live against a Mauga is if she uses her Whipshot to keep you away and Shield Bashes to safety. The only risk you really have as Mauga is if you use Cage Fight in front of her while she is in Rally, as she can cancel it. Don't do that.


Their Perks - Morale Boost can be pretty good against Mauga, as it's fairly easy to hit Whipshot on him and get the sustain. Inspiring Strike can give her more sustain and time alive against Mauga, buying her team time to force you away. Whiplash can be good in some situations, if she's able to knock you into a wall and stun you for a second.


Your Perks - Kinetic Bandolier can be pretty useful against Brigitte, if you're needing to constantly poke her out with your chain guns. Pyromaniac may be a little less effective due to her barrier. Firewalker is a must pick against her, as it is very easy to land an Overrun stomp on Brigitte.

|'''EXCEPTIONAL SYNERGY'''
A fairly unconventional synergy for Brigitte, but Mauga allows her to brawl all out like a maniac with Cardiac Overdrive and her personal sustain potential. Not only that, while she is using Rally she can act as a great form of protection for Mauga using her barrier. They can play very stacked as a unit and have incredible frontline pressure.

|-
!<center>[[Image:icon-illari.png|80px|link=Illari]]<br />[[Illari]]</center>
|'''<nowiki>LOW PRIORITY  |  MEDIUM RISK</nowiki>'''
Illari is good at playing her range and constantly kiting from Mauga due to her mobility. Don't look to fight her too often, as you'll likely end up in a weird position that her team can punish you in. Her pylons are easily breakable using Incendiary Chaingun and its fire effects. If you get close to her, it's game over for her as she has a low hp pool and predictable movement. When she is using Captive Sun, you can look to use Cage Fight and potentially catch her in it, or block the projectile. Otherwise, she isn't too much of a threat besides her range.


Their Perks - Summer Solstice can make Illari harder to track while in Captive Sun, so be careful trying to shoot her if she has it. Solar Flare can provide Illari's team burst sustain that can rival Overdrive, so be careful if she has that as well. Sunburn just provides some extra damage, so track your health pool before engaging on her and be prepared to use Overdrive if needed.


Your Perks - Pyromaniac, Firewalker. Same reasons as Baptiste.

|'''BAD SYNERGY'''
Illari and Mauga don't really mix. They play different tempos and for different things. The only thing they really have going for them is the Cage Fight-Captive Sun combo, which is a guaranteed team wipe a lot of the time.

|-
!<center>[[Image:icon-Jetpack Cat.png|80px|link=Jetpack Cat]]<br />[[Jetpack Cat]]</center>
|'''<nowiki>HIGH PRIORITY | MEDIUM RISK</nowiki>'''
<small>
</small>

|'''TBA SYNERGY'''
<small>
</small>

|-
!<center>[[Image:icon-Juno.png|80px|link=Juno]]<br />[[Juno]]</center>
|'''<nowiki>LOW PRIORITY  |  LOW RISK</nowiki>'''
Juno's mobility makes her incredibly hard to chase down and kill, but she doesn't have much damage or utility to be of threat. Look to poke her with your Incendiary Chaingun and focus on chasing her down when she doesn't have Hyper Ring or Glide Boost. Be careful when she has Orbital Ray, though, as if you slam into her team, even with Overdrive, the damage boost and healing from Orbital Ray can absolutely shut you down. Especially if you use Cage Fight, as you'll be a sitting duck. Pulsar Torpedoes can also be relatively annoying as they do good sustain and have high damage output without much risk for Juno. 
  
Their Perks - Locked On gives Juno a faster Torpedoes cooldown against Mauga, as he doesn't have any way to easily block the torpedoes. Faster Blaster can provide extra sustain and damage for Juno, making her a bit more difficult to deal with. Look to force her Glide Boost early if possible. Lift Off provides Juno a very easy escape to high ground, making it hard to pin her down.
  
Your Perks - Kinetic Bandolier can be good if you're looking to chase her down constantly and need more ammo, but Pyromaniac can also be good if she constantly peeks you and you want some extra overhealth. Firewalker will generally be a good pick as most comps containing Juno play very stacked to get value out of Hyper Ring and Orbital Ray. 

|'''EXCEPTIONAL SYNERGY'''
Mauga and Juno play together very well. Juno's high sustain enables Mauga to stay in the fight for a very long time, as well as her Hyper Ring granting him an insane speed boost for using Overrun. If Mauga uses Cage Fight, it can also be combined with Orbital Ray to create a massive area of sustain and Damage in the Cage, leading to a teamwipe.

|-
!<center>[[Image:icon-kiriko.png|80px|link=Kiriko]]<br />[[Kiriko]]</center>
|'''<nowiki>MEDIUM PRIORITY  |  HIGH RISK</nowiki>'''


Kiriko can be annoying to deal with. High damage, great mobility, and most of all, Protection Suzu being able to clear your burns. Look to poke her out specifically and potentially force her CD's out for your DPS. If she uses her teleport in open space, you can look to run onto her and get an easy kill. Be careful, though, as she can wall climb and escape to a high ground if she needs. If she uses Kitsune Rush, '''run.''' Kitsune is very good at shredding Mauga due to his weak damage mitigation and large hitbox, allowing her to land massive damage alongside her team.


Their Perks - Urgent Care allows her to sustain a teammate you may be dueling a bit faster, potentially stealing your kill. Fortune Teller is very good into Mauga, as it enables her to constantly shoot you but still heal her team.  Foxtrot can enable her teammates to build CD's way faster and potentially outpace you as Mauga. Ready Step is underused, but can enable her to pump insane damage numbers into your noggin.


Your Perks - Pyromaniac can be nice against Kiriko as the constant cleanses from her teleport and Suzu can give you extra overhealth. Depending on the situation, Firewalker can be good, but could also be cleansed completely away by her Suzu. Look to either force it out or pick Combat Fuel if you can't find an opportunity.

|EXCEPTIONAL SYNERGY
Kiriko and Mauga play very well together. High sustain, high damage, and exceptional mobility potential. If you ever get low/have a status effect, Kiriko can use her Protection Suzu to cleanse the effect and grant you essentially a second life. Not only that, Kitsune Rush can provide Mauga insane DPS and two potential uses of Cardiac Overdrive in one fight, a massive advantage over the enemy team. Cage Fight can be combined with Kitsune Rush to confirm a teamfight win nearly every time.

|-
!<center>[[Image:icon-lifeweaver.png|80px|link=Lifeweaver]]<br />[[Lifeweaver]]</center>
|'''<nowiki>HIGH PRIORITY | MEDIUM RISK</nowiki>'''
While Lifeweaver has extremely high sustain and good damage, he doesn't have much else going for him. Look to run past his team and tear him apart, as his very large hitbox makes him an easy target. If he uses Life Grip, you can look to take the space that was given with it. Don't let the fight go on too long, though, as his damage output can actually do a considerable amount to Mauga due to its lack of falloff. If he uses Tree of Life, it's one of the few deployables in the game that can be easily destroyed with Mauga's chainguns. Cage Fight can also be countered with a Life Grip, potentially pulling an enemy caught in the cage out. Pay attention to this, as a lot of teams will look to bait your Cage out early and pull the target out with Grip.


Their Perks - Cleansing Grasp can be annoying, as it will basically give Lifeweaver a permanently shorter Life Grip cooldown if he pulls a target you set on fire. Lifeweaving will also provide more sustain to a target you're shooting, making it harder to eliminate them. Superbloom provides him with even more damage against Mauga, potentially forcing you to back away due to the extra output. Petal Power can be used on a character like Bastion to provide them with an insane DPS boost, forcing you away.


Your Perks - Pyromaniac is a go to here, due to Lifeweaver's large hitbox and lack of good mobility. Firewalker can also be used to damage his Petal Platform and Tree of Life, which can be convenient. If you're unable to get a lot of value out of Firewalker, Combat Fuel can also be useful against a Lifeweaver comp.

|'''OK SYNERGY'''
Lifeweaver can pull you out of sticky situations with his {{al|Life Grip}}. If you can communicate, this can allow you to use your {{al|Overrun}} aggressively more often. Life Grip can also be used to pull Mauga out of his own cage.

A cheeky strategy that can be used with Lifeweaver is to place Cage Fight on top a {{al|Petal Platform}} on the edge of the map, making any enemies caught and Mauga himself fall off the map once the platform is broken. This can be utilized to clear teams instantly depending on how many get caught, however it is tricky to execute as most enemies would avoid getting so close to Mauga. If you do try this, the ally Lifeweaver can use Life Grip to save you from your own ultimate if available.


Cleansing Grasp can also be useful if the enemy team banned Kiriko, giving Mauga a cleanse that can remove Anti-Heals or other status effects.

|-
!<center>[[Image:icon-lúcio.png|80px|link=Lúcio]]<br />[[Lúcio]]</center>
|'''<nowiki>MEDIUM PRIORITY  |  MEDIUM RISK</nowiki>'''
Lucio doesn't typically pose much of a threat to Mauga, and he often plays in a way that makes it very difficult to get near him as Mauga. Look to shoot at him with your Incendiary Chaingun to force him off of speed boost or potentially use Amp It Up. Sound Barrier can be very effective at countering Cage Fight, as the overhealth granted by it can be difficult to get through as Mauga. If you catch Lucio with Cage Fight, though, he becomes very easy to kill due to his inability to Wall Ride.


Their Perks - Soundwave Rider can enable Lucio to boop you off the map more consistently, so be aware of where he is when you go near a ledge. Beat Drop makes it harder to kill people affected by Sound Barrier, as they'll have more move speed or healing until it decays. Noise Violation allows Lucio to play a further range away from Mauga but still get effective Amp It Up value.


Your Perks - Kinetic Bandolier can be useful if you're trying to chase Lucio down, but it's not recommended. Look to just annoy him with poke and use Pyromaniac Overhealth to sustain yourself. Most Lucio compositions will play relatively stacked to get value out of his Crossfade, so Firewalker is a guarantee value pick for your major.

|'''EXCEPTIONAL SYNERGY'''
Lucio is great at enabling any close range hero like Mauga to close distance very quickly. Amp it Up enables crazy movement with Overrun, and also provides ample healing when brawling. Sound Barrier can be used to sustain Mauga in a fight and allow him to play very aggressively. 
Niche Strategy - Cage Fight won't immediately disconnect when someone falls off the map while tethered, so you can have your Lucio boop them off a ledge, then cancel the cage to confirm the kill.

|-
!<center>[[Image:icon-mercy.png|80px|link=Mercy]]<br />[[Mercy]]</center>
|'''<nowiki>LOW PRIORITY  |  MEDIUM RISK</nowiki>'''
Mercy and Mauga don't interact much outside of annoying eachother. Either with Mauga constantly shooting Mercy with his Chainguns, or Mercy damage boosting an individual on her team. Look to shoot her before her pocket target. If she uses Resurrect and is close to the ground, you can either stun it with Overrun or catch her and the res target with Cage Fight.


Their Perks - Angelic Resurrection can make it harder to kill Mercy if you stun her with Overrun. Make sure you pay attention to if she has it and be prepared to deal more damage. Chain Boost can be very oppressive, enabling two targets on her team to deal insane damage towards you. If she has this, play your corners tight and use Overrun to avoid being shot as much. Flash heal can be used to save targets that are low on health, so pay attention to when she uses it and use that as a window of engagement.


Your Perks - Pyromaniac is a good option, considering her predictable movement, but if she plays out of your LOS, Kinetic Bandolier can be better. Combat Fuel will likely see more success as compositions with Mercy tend to play fairly split.

|'''OK SYNERGY'''
Mauga and Mercy don't really mix. Mercy wants to play slow and damage boost someone, and Mauga wants to be a violent brawler who attacks quickly. Mercy and allow Mauga to play more aggressive with her damage boost and potentially resurrect him if he goes for a hyper-aggressive play, but outside of that, not much gets done between the two.

|-
