==Trivia==
[[File:Mauga-weebo.jpg|thumb|Mauga]]
*Instead of using his regular hero portrait, in the battle-pass, Mauga has a unique icon where his mouth is closed instead of his signature cheshire smile.
**It's also worth pointing out his trial-period used a different portrait, with a slightly different angle, and less saturated colors.
*When someone is trapped within Mauga's ultimate, a [[Lifeweaver]] can pull them out of the cage.
*Mauga's chainguns are named "Gunny" and "Cha-Cha."

===Cultural References===
*Mauga is a Samoan name meaning "mountain."
**His last name Malosi derives from Losi, a giant trickster from Samoan mythology
*Mauga's tattoos are a mix of traditional [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pe%CA%BBa tatau] and designs unique to the game.<ref>2023-11-04, [https://www.reddit.com/r/Overwatch/comments/17nisdt/a_quick_run_down_of_maugas_identity_and_voice/ A quick run down of Mauga's identity and voice lines from a Samoan born and raised]. ''Reddit'', accessed on 2023-11-05</ref>
*People often compare Mauga to the ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moana_(2016_film) Moana]'' movie character, Maui. This is due to Mauga having a Polynesian background similar to Maui, and looking somewhat similar to each other (boisterous, able to tank a lot of damage, wild hairstyle, affectionate to their weapons, and jumps greater heights for dramatic flair).
**Interestingly, Mauga's voice actor portrayed Moana's father, Chief Tui, in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moana_(2026_film) 2026 live action adaptation] of that film.
*In the Portuguese version of ''Overwatch'', one of Mauga's chainguns is named "Sasha." Coincidentally or not, this is the same name as the [https://wiki.teamfortress.com/wiki/Heavy Heavy's] chaingun in ''Team Fortress 2''.

===Development===
[[File:Mauga Concept 1.png|thumb|Early Mauga concept art]]
Development on Mauga began in 2018 after the developers saw a piece of concept art.<ref name = "DevelopingSamoan">2024-01-31, [https://www.gamesindustry.biz/developing-overwatch-2s-samoan-hero Developing Overwatch 2's Samoan hero]. ''Games Industry.biz'', accessed on 2024-02-08</ref> Development occurred on-and-off for the following five years. The development team was looking for a character who would fit the archetype of a tank hero with less speed but greater firing power. It was decided that a Samoan could fit this archetype, and the team did research on Samoans and Polynesians, looking for the right look.<ref name = "MakingMauga">2023-12-01, [https://www.rnz.co.nz/international/pacific-news/503702/how-blizzard-created-mauga-a-samoan-hero-in-overwatch-2 How Blizzard created Mauga - a Samoan Hero in Overwatch 2]. ''RNZ'', accessed on 2023-12-06</ref> Blizzard worked with cultural consultants, including artist Si'i Liufau, who specializes in contemporary Polynesian tattoos and Tataus. Liufau called out the initial tattoo the team originally created for Mauga. According to [[Kenny Hudson]], "His [Mauga's] original tattoo was Polynesian inspired but was not done by a true Samoan tattoo artist. We wanted authenticity, and we contracted [Si'i Liufau], a certified master Samoan tattoo artist, and worked hand in hand with him." Liufau drew some stuff up, [[Team 4]] artists drew stuff back, and a middleground was reached due to issues such as rendering. The tattoos that were sketched had such fine details that many game engines couldn't handle it. As such, the middleground was accurate to Samoan culture, but not so detailed that the game couldn't handle it.<ref name = "DevelopingSamoan"/>

Mauga was originally intended to be Hero 31, but as the kit [[Geoff Goodman]] and [[Joshua Noh]] developed came together, they decided it didn't suit Mauga's personality, and instead conceived of an entirely new hero, [[Sigma]], to use it.<ref name="gameplayreveal"/> Development of Sigma forced development of Mauga to take a backseat.<ref name = "DevelopingSamoan"/> In 2019, it was stated that the team still intended to make Mauga a playable hero some day, and had "big plans" for him.<ref name="gameplayreveal">[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8Ez9gD0A0iM&t=1410s Sigma Gameplay Reveal with Seagull and Jeff Kaplan.] ''Youtube'', accessed on 2022-10-12</ref> Mauga's rollout as a hero was further delayed due to the Covid-19 pandemic. By this point, work on Mauga was about 80% complete, but the developers needed more time. As such, Mauga and [[Ramattra]] swapped places in the release order. Originally, Mauga had been planned for [[Season]] 2 and Ramattra Season 8. This was swapped, as by this point, work on Ramattra was complete.<ref name = "DevelopingSamoan"/>

[[File:Mauga Concept 2.png|thumb|left|Ditto]]
In 2022, there was speculation that Mauga would be the hero released for [[Season]] 2 of ''[[Overwatch 2]]''. In June, YouTuber Potxeca claimed developers [[Aaron Keller]] and [[Geoff Goodman]] had told them that Mauga would be released as a hero. It was further speculated that Mauga would be revealed at the 2022 [[Overwatch League]] grand finals, when [[Blizzard Entertainment]] teased a hero reveal.<ref>2022-11-04, [https://www.kotaku.com.au/2022/11/new-overwatch-2-hero-to-appear-at-owl-finals-fans-think-its-mauga/ New Overwatch 2 Hero To Appear At OWL Finals, Fans Think It’s Mauga]. ''Kotaku'', accessed on 2022-11-06</ref> Instead, however, [[Ramattra]] was the hero revealed at the event.<ref name="firstnews">2022-11-05, [https://overwatch.blizzard.com/en-us/news/23876523/ Ramattra Reveal - Overwatch League Grand Finals.] ''Overwatch News'', accessed on 2022-11-06</ref> 

[[File:Overwatch-2-mauga-concept-art-02.webp|thumb|Mauga final concept art]]
It was reported by GameSpot that a Tank hero would be released in Season 7+, and it would be an [[omnic]].<ref name="UpdateRoadmap">2023-05-16, [https://www.gamespot.com/articles/overwatch-2s-update-roadmap-features-new-characters-story-missions-and-reworks/1100-6514243/ Overwatch 2's Update Roadmap Features New Characters, Story Missions, And Reworks]. ''GameSpot'', accessed on 2023-05-20</ref> While the Tank report was accurate, the omnic claim was not.

For [[Season]] 7, it was announced that a new [[Control]] map named "[[Samoa]]" would be released. This led to speculation that Mauga would be released as a hero in Season 8.<ref>2023-09-27, [https://www.dexerto.com/overwatch/overwatch-2-players-convinced-new-samoa-map-confirms-mauga-as-next-tank-hero-2311099/ Overwatch 2 players convinced new Samoa map confirms Mauga as next tank hero]. ''Dexerto'', accessed on 2023-10-04</ref> Mauga was leaked hours prior to his official reveal at [[BlizzCon 2023]] on the Nintendo e-shop.<ref>2023-11-04, [https://www.kotaku.com.au/2023/11/overwatch-2-introduces-new-tank-hero-mauga-at-blizzcon-2023/ Overwatch 2 Introduces New Tank Hero Mauga At BlizzCon 2023]. ''Kotaku'', accessed on 2023-11-04</ref>

====Ability Development====
The developers tried a few alternate mobility abilities for Overrun. One of the first ideas was a short range dash that would toss enemies into the air behind Mauga if he impacted them. 

Mauga's weapons weren't always miniguns. There were a few alternates tested such as a flamethrower or incendiary grenade launchers. There were a few attempts at having two very different firing weapons in each hand, with one being hitscan and the other being a projectile. This didn't play well when trying to fire both at the same time, as the weapons had different firing rates, and aiming projectiles was difficult. Furthermore, the player was required to track the ammo pools separately, which was also difficult.

Mauga's Cage Fight differs little in the final version from its inceptions. However, the developers still tried other versions to see what would play best. It was a physical wall instead of a barrier at one point. There was also a completely different ult that was more of an area effect debuff to enemy damage dealt, the opposite of damage boost.<ref>2023-12-12, [https://www.reddit.com/r/Overwatch/comments/18g8m6p/comment/kd0zw2z/?context=3%5D We're the Overwatch 2 hero design team, and we'll be here tomorrow at 11:00 AM PT to answer questions about Mauga's first week in-game!]. ''Reddit'', accessed on 2023-12-16</ref>

